  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe part-solid law reports `RapidInPart` when the tool meets the part on a rapid move.\nThe message names the move.\nThe stock law keeps its message.\nBoth findings block the post.\nMCP reports `rapid_in_part`.\nThe UI keeps part and stock findings in separate groups with their move locations.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe part-solid law used `RapidInStock` for contact with the part.\nIts message described stock and the clearance plane, including on vertical lifts and drops.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe images show the diagnostics of one operation that has stock rapids and part rapids.\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/e0928e6c1ce8b593220b54dac709a16829513961/pr-3777/before.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/e0928e6c1ce8b593220b54dac709a16829513961/pr-3777/after.png) |\n\n- Before: one group. The part rapids have the stock message (\"repeated on 2 more moves (to 6)\").\n- After: two groups. The stock rapid (move 3) keeps the stock message. The part rapids (moves 4 and 6) have the message \"tool meets the part on rapid move 4\".\n\nThe images are on the `pr-screenshots` branch of the fork, at commit `e0928e6c1`.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe final head is `e1bbe8583f9a867d8465f69c00dff93894a726eb`.\nIt contains a merge of `upstream/main` at `db3bb1f7f3c47cf3561a8e9534f4f2cde260cba8`.\nAll results below are from that head, on a macOS host with a working graphics adapter.\n\n- Pins, in `crates/sim/tests/posed_rapids.rs`, module `part_message`:\n  - `a_vertical_part_rapid_names_the_part_and_move`\n  - `a_stack_retract_edge_column_names_the_part_and_move`\n  - `a_stopped_fine_bore_holder_rapid_names_the_part_and_move`\n  - `a_stock_rapid_keeps_its_stock_message`\n- Pin proof: I reverted each producer in `crates/sim/src/verify/solid.rs` to `RapidInStock`, one at a time.\n  - Line 220 (stopped fine-bore body): `a_stopped_fine_bore_holder_rapid_names_the_part_and_move` FAILED. Restored: passed.\n  - Line 231 (retract edge column): `a_stack_retract_edge_column_names_the_part_and_move` FAILED. Restored: passed.\n  - Line 236 (general rapid): `a_vertical_part_rapid_names_the_part_and_move` FAILED. Restored: passed.\n- The stock control keeps its original message and blocking result.\n- MCP kind and UI grouping, location, and severity have structural pins.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green; 411 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n  - `ui lib`: 1,537 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored. `headless_run_succeeds` and the report tests passed.\n  - `app suites: rotary_verify`: 10 passed, 0 failed.\n  - `sim suites: posed_rapids`: 9 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: green; 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: green; 99 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n- App `example_catalog` (39 passed, 4 ignored), `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `first_part_programs`, `first_router_part` and `solid_law_goldens` passed in the quick gate.\n\nThe heavy gate checked four existing expected failures: three for #1950 and one for #2849.\nEach was red as expected. No unexpected failure occurred.\n\n`upstream/main` moved to `29bb9e9a2` (PR #3797, a Machines pane fix) after the gates started.\n`git merge-tree` shows that this head merges cleanly with it.\n\n## Test placement\n\nThis PR adds no top-level test binary.\nThe four pins are in the existing binary `crates/sim/tests/posed_rapids.rs`, which holds the part and stock rapid laws.\n`crates/sim/tests/` has no directory suite at this time.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog and reached golden suites passed on the final head.\nThe diff changes no `*.nc` file, no `*.cl` file and no file in `examples/catalog/`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo manual GUI session ran.\nNo real CNC machine ran this change.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPRs #3251 and #3103 touch the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Rapid contact with the part names the part and move instead of describing stock below the clearance plane.\n\nFixes #3520\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
